course: dictionary
lesson: 2374
title: The first writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long ago, people did not have books or paper. Some of the first writing was made in ancient Mesopotamia, in what is now Iraq. The writers, called scribes, pressed a cut reed into wet clay to make it.
explain: The marks were small and shaped like wedges. «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay, making wedge-shaped marks called cuneiform.» So cuneiform is the name of this writing, and the sentence tells you what its marks look like.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it in. The second sentence says «the word cuneiform means wedge-shaped», so cuneiform is a kind of writing made of wedges. You can also use it as a describing word, as in a cuneiform tablet.
fact: Cuneiform is one of the oldest kinds of writing in the world.
fact: It was first used in ancient Mesopotamia, now Iraq, over 5,000 years ago.
fact: Scribes made the marks by pressing a reed into wet clay, so the marks were wedge-shaped.
fact: At first cuneiform was used for counting grain, animals and taxes, and later for laws, letters and stories like the Epic of Gilgamesh.
fact: Clay tablets with cuneiform can be seen in museums such as the British Museum.
exercise: «Scribes pressed a cut reed into wet clay, making wedge-shaped marks.» What were the marks shaped like? | Circles | *Wedges | Waves | Stars
exercise: Where was cuneiform first used? | Ancient Egypt, beside the Nile | Ancient China | *Ancient Mesopotamia, now Iraq | Ancient Rome
exercise: Which of these was cuneiform used for at first? | Painting pictures on walls | Playing games | Making paper aeroplanes | *Counting grain and animals
test: What does the adjective cuneiform describe? | *Something shaped like a wedge, or written in this script | A king's name | A river in Iraq | A cut reed
test: Where can you see clay tablets with cuneiform? | A swimming pool | *The British Museum | A football stadium | A supermarket
exam: Which statement is true? | Cuneiform was first used in London | Cuneiform is a kind of food | Cuneiform is a newer kind of writing made with pens | *Cuneiform was made by pressing a reed into wet clay
